Rule 1 (strict elementwise shape match to avoid size mismatch)
{v_1 : tensor, v_2 : tensor, v_3 : tensor} |= ndim(v_1) = ndim(v_2) ∧ ndim(v_1) = ndim(v_3) ∧ ∀i ∈ [0, ndim(v_1) - 1] : shape(v_1, i) = shape(v_2, i) ∧ shape(v_1, i) = shape(v_3, i) ∧ shape(v_1, i) ≥ 1
>>
Rule 2 (inputs share the same dtype to prevent unintended promotions)
{v_1 : tensor, v_2 : tensor, v_3 : tensor} |= dtype_(v_1) = dtype_(v_2) ∧ dtype_(v_1) = dtype_(v_3)
>>
Rule 3 (out tensor matches input tensor in dtype and shape to avoid cast errors)
{v_1 : tensor, v_5 : tensor} |= dtype_(v_5) = dtype_(v_1) ∧ ndim(v_5) = ndim(v_1) ∧ ∀i ∈ [0, ndim(v_1) - 1] : shape(v_5, i) = shape(v_1, i)
>>
Rule 5 (float value path with aligned shapes)
{v_1 : tensor, v_2 : tensor, v_3 : tensor, v_4 : float} |= v_4 ≥ 0 ∧ ndim(v_1) = ndim(v_2) ∧ ndim(v_1) = ndim(v_3) ∧ ∀i ∈ [0, ndim(v_1) - 1] : shape(v_1, i) = shape(v_2, i) ∧ shape(v_1, i) = shape(v_3, i)
